<title>
Precautions for Diagnosing Trouble
</title>
<list1 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Diagnose blind spot monitor system according to the procedure in 
<intxref refid = "AENLSB0AAA24001">Blind Spot Monitor System Check:Blind Spot Monitor</intxref>
.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that component parts related to the vehicle posture such as tires, suspension, etc. are standard parts.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that rear bumper is standard parts and well installed.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that blind spot monitor control modules are installed in the original position.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
Check that rear bumper around blind spot monitor control module is in the following conditions.
</ptxt>
</item>
<list2 type = "unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>
Sticker, film, etc. are not affixed or paint is not adhered.
</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>
There is no abrasion or adhesion of dirt, etc. on the surface.
</ptxt>
</item>
</list2>
<item>
<ptxt>
When checking blind spot monitor control module (1) for terminal voltage or waveform, connect service wires (3) between the control module and disconnected connector (2).
</ptxt>
<figure>
